From: Tiberiu Chibici <chibicitiberiu@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 01:28:23 +0300
Subject: rdatawad: write the DMX format field little-endian

wav_to_doom() stored the DMX header's format field as a host-order 3, while the rate is
swapped with SHORT() and the length is copied from the little-endian WAV header. Built on a
big-endian host (Debian's ppc64 and powerpc builds run rdatawad natively), every sound lump in
dsda-doom.wad starts 00 03 instead of 03 00, so the game's IsDMXSound() check fails and the
lump is handed to libsndfile, which knows no DMX: "sf_open_virtual: Format not recognised.
Can't open sfx file" for dsdgsit, dsdgatk, dsdgact, dsdgdth and dsdgpain (the helper dog's
sounds, the only sounds in dsda-doom.wad). Little-endian builds are unchanged.

Forwarded: no

diff --git a/prboom2/data/rd_sound.c b/prboom2/data/rd_sound.c
--- a/prboom2/data/rd_sound.c
+++ b/prboom2/data/rd_sound.c
@@ -67,7 +67,9 @@ size_t wav_to_doom(void **lumpdata, const char *filename)
   size = sizeof(*out) - 1 + LONG(header->datalen);
   out = xmalloc(size);
 
-  out->log2bits = 3;
+  // the lump is little-endian like the WAV file: format 3 (DMX), the rate
+  // swapped to little-endian, the length copied as is (little-endian already)
+  out->log2bits = SHORT(3);
   out->rate = SHORT(LONG(header->samplerate));
   out->length = header->datalen;
   memmove(out->samples, header->samples, LONG(header->datalen));
